<h1>Maintenance Windows</h1>
<p>A maintenance window is a period of time during which SITE_NAME withholds alerts
for some or all checks in a project. Use maintenance windows for planned work,
such as database upgrades or server reboots, when you expect jobs to miss their
schedules and do not want to be paged about it.</p>
<h2>What a Maintenance Window Does</h2>
<p>While a maintenance window is active, the checks it covers work as usual:
they keep receiving pings, and they keep changing status (for example, from "up"
to "down" when a ping is late). The only difference is that SITE_NAME does not
send notifications about these status changes.</p>
<ul>
<li>A window starts at its start time (inclusive) and ends at its end time
  (exclusive).</li>
<li>A window covers either <strong>all checks</strong> in the project, or only the
  <strong>checks having all of the listed tags</strong>. Tag matching is exact and
  case-sensitive: a window with the tags <code>db prod</code> covers a check tagged
  <code>db prod www</code>, but not a check tagged <code>db</code> or <code>DB prod</code>.</li>
<li>A check can be covered by several overlapping windows at the same time.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What Happens When a Window Ends</h2>
<p>When the last maintenance window covering a check ends, and the check is still
down, SITE_NAME sends <strong>one</strong> "down" alert for it. The <code>sendalerts</code> process sends
this alert within 60 seconds after the window ends.</p>
<ul>
<li>If a check went down and then came back up during the window, SITE_NAME
  sends no alerts for it: both the "down" alert and the matching "up" alert
  are withheld.</li>
<li>If SITE_NAME withheld a check's "down" alert, it also withholds the "up" alert
  that follows it, so you never receive an "up" alert without the
  "down" alert before it.</li>
<li>Hourly and daily email reminders about down checks
  (see <a href="../configuring_notifications/">Configuring Notifications</a>) skip checks that
  are covered by an active maintenance window.</li>
</ul>
<p>Each withheld alert shows up in the check's event log as
<strong>Alert not sent: maintenance window "&lt;name&gt;"</strong>, where &lt;name&gt; is
the name of the window that covered the check.</p>
<h2>Limits</h2>
<ul>
<li>A project can have at most 100 upcoming and active maintenance windows.</li>
<li>A maintenance window can be at most 30 days long.</li>
<li>SITE_NAME automatically deletes ended maintenance windows 90 days after
  their end time.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Managing Maintenance Windows in the Dashboard</h2>
<p>Open the <strong>Maintenance</strong> page from the project's navigation bar. On this page
you can:</p>
<ul>
<li>Schedule a maintenance window for a future time with <strong>Schedule Maintenance</strong>.</li>
<li>Start a maintenance window immediately with <strong>Start Now</strong>.</li>
<li>Edit or remove upcoming windows, and end active windows early.</li>
</ul>
<p>On each check's details page, the <strong>Start Maintenance</strong> button opens a form that
starts a maintenance window immediately. The form is pre-filled to cover the checks
having all of this check's tags (or all checks, if this check has no tags).</p>
<h2>Managing Maintenance Windows with the API</h2>
<p>Deploy scripts can open and close maintenance windows using the
<a href="../api/#list-maintenance">Management API</a>. The API lets you list, create, get,
end early, and delete maintenance windows. For example, a deploy script can
create a window with a 30-minute duration before starting a deployment, and end
it once the deployment has finished.</p>
<h2>Notes for Self-Hosted Instances</h2>
<p>Maintenance windows rely on the <code>manage.py sendalerts</code> management command: it
both withholds alerts during maintenance and sends the deferred alerts after
the windows end. If you self-host SITE_NAME, make sure <code>sendalerts</code> is running.</p>
<p>To find withheld alerts that have not yet been released (for example, because
<code>sendalerts</code> was not running when a window ended), query the <code>api_flip</code> table:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code><span class="k">SELECT</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">*</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">FROM</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">api_flip</span>
<span class="k">WHERE</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">withheld</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">IS</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">NOT</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">NULL</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">AND</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="n">withheld_outcome</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">IS</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="k">NULL</span><span class="p">;</span>
</code></pre></div>